":"lower","call":"Under 3.5 goals","text":"The numbers say 3.2 goals, which looks a little high. Heerenveen have conceded only four in their last six and have kept five clean sheets this season. Feyenoord are without Jeremiah St. Juste, Gijs Smal, Thomas Beelen, Bart Nieuwkoop, Jordan Bos and Jakub Moder, but they have also scored less than expected lately after a demanding European week."},"corners":{"lean":"same","call":"Around 10 corners","text":"The numbers say 9.8 corners, slightly more for Feyenoord. Heerenveen play a 4-2-3-1 with full-backs who push forward, so both sides should win corners, which is what the model already expects. Nothing points clearly away from it."},"cards":{"lean":"same","call":"Around 2-3 cards","text":"The numbers say 2.6 cards, with Danny Makkelie refereeing. He shows fewer cards than most Eredivisie referees, and we found no suspensions or disciplinary news for either side. A frustrated Feyenoord could add a booking, but not enough to move away from the model."},"shots":{"lean":"same","call":"Around 29 shots","text":"The numbers say 29.4 shots. Veldman calls Feyenoord a side that creates many chances, and his own team keeps attacking at home with Jacob Trenskow and Dylan Vente. Against that, Feyenoord may be tired after Inter, so the two effects roughly cancel out."},"shots_on_target":{"lean":"lower","call":"Under 9.5 shots on target","text":"The numbers say 9.7 shots on target. Heerenveen have allowed only 14 shots on target in their last six games, about half the expected number, and Feyenoord lacked a cutting edge against Inter. Shaqueel van Persie is only just returning to fitness, so we expect slightly fewer efforts on target than the model."},"sources":["https://www.feanonline.nl/veldman-verwacht-zware-middag-tegen-feyenoord-een-mooie-test/","https://www.fr-fans.nl/nieuws/79800/een-oude-bekende-een-opvallende-ommekeer-en-een-plek-waar-feyenoord-zelden-plezier-beleeft","https://www.fr-fans.nl/nieuws/79790/van-bronckhorst-geeft-u